    <!-- Guide / tutorial tab -->
    <string name="tutorial_header">How to use Svartifoss</string>
    <string name="tutorial_intro">Svartifoss turns your watch into a remote for the music playing on your phone. Here\'s everything you can do from your wrist.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_taps_title">Tap the screen zones</string>
    <string name="tutorial_taps_desc">The watch screen is split into four zones — top, bottom, left and right. Tapping a zone runs the action you assigned to it. By default the left zone plays or pauses, the right skips to the next track, and the top and bottom change the volume.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_gestures_title">Single, double &amp; long press</string>
    <string name="tutorial_gestures_desc">Each zone holds three separate actions: one for a single tap, one for a double tap and one for a long press. For example, a single tap in the center can pause the music while a double tap opens the actions menu — you won\'t see this unless you set it up, so customize it to taste.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_buttons_title">Physical buttons</string>
    <string name="tutorial_buttons_desc">If your watch has side buttons, you can assign single, double and long-press actions to them too. They keep working even when the screen is off.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_rotary_title">Rotating crown</string>
    <string name="tutorial_rotary_desc">Turn the rotating crown or bezel to change the volume. Prefer to scrub through the song instead? Turn on “Seek with rotary crown” in Settings.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_swipe_up_title">Swipe up, down, left &amp; right</string>
    <string name="tutorial_swipe_up_desc">Swipe up, down or left on the now-playing screen can each be configured to open anything — the actions menu, the playback queue, skip tracks, your playlists, and more. Configure each one in Playing controls / Stopped controls, under \"Swipe gestures\". By default, swiping up opens the actions menu and the others do nothing until you assign them. Swipe right is left alone — that\'s the universal Wear OS gesture to exit the app.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_yt_music_title">YouTube Music shortcuts</string>
    <string name="tutorial_yt_music_desc">Assign \"Play liked songs\", \"Play liked songs, shuffled\" or \"My playlists\" to any button, gesture or swipe to jump straight into your music without touching the phone. \"Search history\" remembers your recent searches on the watch — press and hold one to delete it.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_exit_title">Swipe to exit</string>
    <string name="tutorial_exit_desc">Swipe from the left edge to leave the player. It can pause playback automatically when you exit — enable it in Settings.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_tile_title">Quick-control Tile</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tile_desc">Swipe the watch face sideways to the Svartifoss tile for instant play, pause and skip without opening the app.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_complication_title">Watch face complication</string>
    <string name="tutorial_complication_desc">Add the Svartifoss album art complication to your watch face to see the current cover at a glance. Tap it to open the player.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_system_title">System media controls</string>
    <string name="tutorial_system_desc">The current track also shows up in your watch\'s own media controls and recent apps, so you can control playback from there as well.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_tip">Tip: set up every gesture in the Playing, Stopped and Actions tabs.</string>

